abstract: "For a smooth positive density on a closed manifold embedded in Euclidean space with the fixed cost |x-y|^2, the Sinkhorn metric operator converges in operator norm to the inverse weighted Laplacian (rate O(eps^(1/2)) in L2 operator norm, O(eps) from H2 to L2), and the metric has the first correction -(eps/4) int <Q grad phi, grad phi> dmu with Q the sum of squared shape operators: a nonpositive, embedding-dependent bias (chord shorter than arc). A positive correction removes it; the expansions hold along smooth density families; spheres are solved exactly to second order; a circle high-frequency family rules out operator-norm rates better than O(eps). Operator-level curvature expansions are credited to prior work. Population densities only; unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only; scripts are floating-point checks. Text CC0-1.0; code MIT."
